    "notes": "John inherited Hainaut from his grandmother Margaret in 1280, completing the effective transition to the House of Avesnes. In 1299 he also inherited Holland and Zeeland, creating a personal union with Hainaut. The requested label 'John I of Hainaut (1247–1304)' is not the usual Hainaut numbering. This ruler is normally John II of Hainaut and John I of Holland. His father John I of Avesnes was Margaret II of Flanders's son and had obtained the Avesnes claim to Hainaut but died in 1257, before John II became sole count in 1280.",
